WEBVTT

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:06.750
On that day, like what all passionate soccer players yearn for,

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:11.120
we stood on the pitch of FC Barcelona's Camp Nou.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.670
There, by playing our own unique brand of soccer,

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:21.730
we shocked the whole world!{and we shall shock the world! }

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:55.760
The Furuyas?{Lines 5-17 are flashback from ep 2, so kept same for consistency. -sm}

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:58.660
They're the core of the Predators.

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:01.500
They're known as the Triplet Demons.

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:03.570
Triplet Demons?

00:02:03.570 --> 00:02:07.140
They're really good, but their personalities...

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:09.510
Yo, isn't that Shou-kun?

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:11.510
Hey, long time no see.

00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:14.110
I have something to tell you three.

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:19.320
Can't you tell? We're in the middle of tennis practice.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:22.220
Can you just hear us out?

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:26.060
Shut up! You're disturbing us!

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:28.730
What's with that attitude!?

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:49.620
Shou-kun!

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:56.020
Hey!

00:02:56.020 --> 00:02:57.690
W-Wait.

00:02:57.690 --> 00:03:00.130
I'm fine.

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:05.400
「The Triplet Demons」

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:05.400
「The Triplet Demons」

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:03.160
Sorry for getting in the way of your tennis practice.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:06.300
But Kota-kun, your kick was amazing.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.970
Playing tennis is such a waste.

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:10.840
You should be playing soccer, right?

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:11.740
Huh?

00:03:11.740 --> 00:03:14.010
Is this what you came here for?{Is this what you wanted to tell us?}

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:18.680
We won't be playing soccer under that terrible coach.

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:20.710
Right, Kota?

00:03:20.710 --> 00:03:22.080
No!

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:26.650
We're trying to create a new team, 
and we want to recruit the three of you.

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:27.720
We?

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:30.690
Yes! Me and Erika-chan.

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:33.760
Let me introduce her. She's Takatou Erika-chan.

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:37.130
She played soccer on a girls' team in Osaka.

00:03:37.130 --> 00:03:40.870
Oh? We're playing with a girl?

00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:45.940
Ouzou-kun, didn't you say her shot was pretty good for a girl?

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:47.010
I guess.

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:49.580
Erika-chan's a lot better than me.

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:50.710
Obviously.{That's for sure.}

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:53.850
How about it? Won't you join our team?

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:58.950
We can play games with New Tokyo FC Rosa's feeder teams.

00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:01.390
Rosa? The team in the Nadeshiko League?

00:04:01.390 --> 00:04:04.520
I know Shimizu Misaki, a player on Rosa.

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:07.160
She told me to form my team.

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:08.460
Feeder teams?

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:10.930
Female youth teams.

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:12.330
Well...

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:13.670
What's with that?

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:15.930
Kota-kun is saying that there's not much point in this.

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:18.840
We should be playing Rosa, the top team.

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:20.070
We can!

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:23.410
If we beat the feeder teams, we can play Rosa!

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:24.780
Really?

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:27.650
Yep! They'll let us play if we win.

00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:29.280
Let's do it, then.

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:30.520
Really?

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:31.880
If that's what Kota-kun wants.

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:35.420
You're right. A top-flight women's team sounds like an interesting opponent.

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:37.290
Are these guys serious?

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:39.490
Yes! Now we have five people!

00:04:39.490 --> 00:04:42.360
Oh yeah. Erika-chan, let me introduce them properly.

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:47.270
Furuya Kota-kun, Furuya Ryuuji-kun, and Furuya Ouzou-kun.

00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:50.200
They do look alike.

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:51.670
You just have to get used to it.

00:04:51.670 --> 00:04:54.040
We only have five people here.

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:56.040
What do we do for the remaining six?

00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:59.010
Just eight is fine for now, so we need three more.

00:04:59.010 --> 00:05:01.050
I have just the three.

00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:03.850
The 3U?

00:05:03.850 --> 00:05:05.250
3U?

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:08.620
Uchimura-kun, Uematsu-kun, and Ukishima-kun.

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:11.320
Their last names start with U, so 3U.

00:05:12.090 --> 00:05:15.090
Those three will do, I guess.

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:29.170
Those three are pretty good.

00:05:29.170 --> 00:05:30.310
See?

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:33.780
But is it really okay to leave it to the three of them?

00:05:33.780 --> 00:05:39.420
No problem. 3U left the team because the Furuyas left.

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:44.190
They have to prepare for exams,
 but they'll agree if the triplets ask them.

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:49.290
So you're using the triplets to gather more members?

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:50.960
Nice.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:55.670
Looks like they've agreed.

00:05:55.670 --> 00:05:58.440
Thank you, everyone!

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:02.840
Now that all of you are here, the new team is born!

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:04.510
Thank you again!

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:06.850
Can we really play against Rosa?

00:06:06.850 --> 00:06:08.310
If we beat the youth teams.

00:06:08.310 --> 00:06:09.550
We will.

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:11.020
You make it sound so simple.

00:06:11.020 --> 00:06:14.290
Of course, we need proper training.

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:17.890
If we can't play against Rosa, 
there's no point in making this team.{If we can't play against Rosa, then why did we even create this team?}

00:06:17.890 --> 00:06:19.560
Of course.

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:24.000
Let's start practicing tomorrow after school at Misaki Park. Okay?

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:26.900
I'll find someone to have a practice match with.

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:28.670
Sure, but what's our team name?

00:06:28.670 --> 00:06:30.440
I haven't decided yet.

00:06:30.440 --> 00:06:31.870
It doesn't matter, does it?

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:34.310
I want a cool name.

00:06:34.310 --> 00:06:36.410
Dandelion!

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:38.180
Dandelion?

00:06:38.180 --> 00:06:39.580
The flower.

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:40.980
What's this?

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:44.350
A poster I have of the Namba Dandelions.

00:06:44.350 --> 00:06:46.850
A flower born in the wild, with a lion's heart...

00:06:46.850 --> 00:06:50.590
That's right. That's the slogan for the team.

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:51.660
Pretty cool, right?

00:06:53.360 --> 00:06:55.160
Looks pretty strong.

00:06:55.160 --> 00:06:57.900
"Someday, we'll be number one in the world!" That's pretty nice, too.

00:06:57.900 --> 00:06:59.500
Sounds good.

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:02.070
Okay! We're the Dandelions!

00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:04.100
The Momoyama Dandelions!

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:09.540
Is the Dandelions' team practice really that interesting?

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:12.580
Yes! We started only three days ago, though.

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:16.580
How should I put this? Up until now, the coach used to decide our positions.

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:18.180
But us...

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:25.890
Erika-chan, shoot!

00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:29.630
Yes! Nice shot!

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:33.500
That shot was pretty pro, wasn't it?

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:36.700
Okay, I pretty much got it.

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:38.540
We should decide on positions.

00:07:38.540 --> 00:07:42.670
That's right. We can tell what Erika-san's good at.

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:45.540
We know her playing style as well.{We know how she can kick the ball.}

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:50.150
Ukishima-kun has pretty good reflexes, so I think he can play any position.

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:52.480
But can you be our goalkeeper this time?

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:54.390
I knew that from the start.{I knew it.}

00:07:54.390 --> 00:07:56.420
Ouzou-kun will be the heart of our defense.

00:07:56.420 --> 00:07:57.560
Okay.

00:07:57.560 --> 00:08:02.730
Shou-kun, you'll be playing defense, too. Try not to trip up Ouzou-kun too much.

00:08:02.730 --> 00:08:03.660
Okay!

00:08:04.700 --> 00:08:07.230
Uchimura-kun and I will be the midfielders.

00:08:07.230 --> 00:08:11.170
When we get pressured, one of us will fall back and play as the third back.

00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:17.780
Kota-kun is the center forward. Erika-san will play 
left forward, and Uematsu-kun will play right forward.

00:08:17.780 --> 00:08:20.480
I can only kick with my right foot, though.

00:08:20.480 --> 00:08:22.280
That's no problem.

00:08:22.280 --> 00:08:27.150
Just cut into the middle like you just did and shoot with your right.

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:31.960
Kota-kun will be yelling at you to pass, but just play however you want.

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:34.830
So we decided the positions ourselves.

00:08:34.830 --> 00:08:37.430
It all feels so fresh.

00:08:37.430 --> 00:08:41.070
It's interesting how we can get so much done even without a coach.

00:08:41.070 --> 00:08:42.170
That's great.

00:08:42.170 --> 00:08:47.240
Yep! Those triplets may seem a bit cocky,

00:08:47.240 --> 00:08:49.710
but their skills are for real.

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:51.380
Things should get very interesting.

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:53.650
You're still eating?

00:08:53.650 --> 00:08:57.880
Got a problem with that? Eating fast is not healthy for you.

00:08:57.880 --> 00:09:00.520
I finished my other task.

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:04.490
I went over to the neighboring middle school and arranged a match with their soccer club.

00:09:04.490 --> 00:09:05.760
A middle school club?

00:09:06.930 --> 00:09:09.490
You went off campus on your own again?

00:09:12.730 --> 00:09:14.670
A match with middle schoolers?

00:09:14.670 --> 00:09:17.570
Yep! They're 7th and 8th graders.

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:19.740
But they'll be pretty big.

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:23.110
That's why he asked them.

00:09:23.110 --> 00:09:24.540
Why?

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:27.150
We are aiming to play the top-flight Rosa.

00:09:27.150 --> 00:09:28.680
In other words, against adults.

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:33.690
They may be women, but they have the physical upper hand against us.

00:09:33.690 --> 00:09:36.690
That's why we're practicing against middle schoolers.

00:09:36.690 --> 00:09:38.420
I see.

00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:39.830
When are we playing?

00:09:39.830 --> 00:09:42.430
We agreed on one week later.

00:09:42.430 --> 00:09:44.960
We have to muscle up in one week?

00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:46.870
No.

00:09:46.870 --> 00:09:50.240
There's no point in trying to increase our physical strength pointlessly.

00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:51.870
Then what do we do?

00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:56.210
I have a video I want to show all of you.{I have some tape I want to show all of you.}

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:01.150
Misaki-san!

00:10:01.150 --> 00:10:05.050
That's right. This is the video of Rosa when they were playing in America.

00:10:05.050 --> 00:10:08.150
Their opponents seem pretty tough. A pro female team?

00:10:08.150 --> 00:10:11.060
Yep. A professional team on the west coast.

00:10:11.060 --> 00:10:14.290
Their physical size makes it seem like a men versus women match.

00:10:16.230 --> 00:10:18.330
American female players are amazing!

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:21.070
No, Rosa is the amazing side.

00:10:21.070 --> 00:10:22.300
How?

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:24.000
The real thing starts now.{Just keep watching.}

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:26.640
Watch carefully. You can learn a lot.

00:10:27.340 --> 00:10:28.470
Misaki-san, she...

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:34.810
The coach gave some instructions.

00:10:34.810 --> 00:10:37.250
This is when they change their playing style.

00:10:44.390 --> 00:10:46.160
You're right.

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:50.100
They aren't keeping the ball at their feet. They're passing immediately.

00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:54.800
They see the pressing opponents, so they pass after playing only one or two touches on the ball.

00:10:56.230 --> 00:10:57.800
Now they're on offense.

00:11:01.540 --> 00:11:02.810
And all of a sudden...

00:11:11.080 --> 00:11:12.280
Yes!

00:11:12.280 --> 00:11:14.450
Goal!

00:11:14.450 --> 00:11:19.560
With only four direct passes, Misaki got her goal.

00:11:19.560 --> 00:11:20.860
Do you get it?

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:26.360
Before the opponent closes in on you, pass the ball around, then attack!

00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:29.970
The ball will go into the goal as long as they keep this up.

00:11:29.970 --> 00:11:31.970
That's not all.

00:11:31.970 --> 00:11:33.910
The opponent will get frustrated.

00:11:33.910 --> 00:11:36.940
That's when we'll get more chances.

00:11:36.940 --> 00:11:38.040
I see.

00:11:38.040 --> 00:11:40.810
This is how we play against players bigger than us?

00:11:40.810 --> 00:11:47.020
We'll practice passing the ball around and counterattacking tomorrow.

00:11:55.260 --> 00:11:59.000
Hey! If you're marked, pass it out quickly!

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:04.240
Over here!

00:12:06.340 --> 00:12:08.470
Erika-chan, that pass came out too slowly!

00:12:08.470 --> 00:12:10.540
But I had no passing lanes!

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:12.410
Ryuuji was behind you.

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:15.950
Before you receive a pass, pay attention to where your teammates are.

00:12:15.950 --> 00:12:17.750
You have to look around you.

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:21.090
The players on Rosa will stick to you even closer.

00:12:22.320 --> 00:12:25.590
Shut up! I'll just keep my eyes wide open, then!{Shut up! I'll open my eyes wide, then!}

00:12:28.830 --> 00:12:30.030
He's coming!

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:33.770
Ow...

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:34.670
Sorry.

00:12:34.670 --> 00:12:36.100
It's all right, so just let your voice out!

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:36.870
Yeah.

00:12:36.870 --> 00:12:38.400
Hey! Go!

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:41.840
Middle school students are huge!

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:44.610
I can't be scared.

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:46.680
Erika-chan, there's space!

00:12:54.090 --> 00:12:55.420
It's going just like our practice!

00:12:59.020 --> 00:12:59.960
Go!

00:13:08.400 --> 00:13:10.400
Yes!

00:13:10.400 --> 00:13:11.900
Nice header!

00:13:46.100 --> 00:13:48.140
We're amazing!

00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:50.110
It went so well!

00:13:50.110 --> 00:13:51.710
That surprised me.

00:13:51.710 --> 00:13:53.480
They're middle schoolers, too!

00:13:53.480 --> 00:13:56.450
I got a hat trick!

00:13:56.450 --> 00:13:57.950
Amazing!

00:13:57.950 --> 00:14:01.250
Looks like we're ready to play against Rosa now.

00:14:01.250 --> 00:14:03.560
Shou-kun, please contact them.

00:14:03.560 --> 00:14:05.560
All right. I'll ask right away.

00:14:05.560 --> 00:14:08.030
Kota-kun, it's finally time.

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:09.190
Yeah.

00:14:09.930 --> 00:14:12.300
Thank you very much.

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:16.970
Oh? Your team name's The Momoyama Dandelions?

00:14:16.970 --> 00:14:20.540
Yes! "A flower born in the wild, with a lion's heart!"

00:14:21.610 --> 00:14:22.910
You're triplets?

00:14:22.910 --> 00:14:26.140
Whoa! I'm being stared at with three of the same faces!

00:14:26.140 --> 00:14:30.650
We aren't really staring. We're just very excited.

00:14:31.820 --> 00:14:37.060
Cosmos! Please play a mini game with them. No need to hold back.

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:38.120
Okay!

00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:42.260
We Rosas will be on pitch #1 over there. See you later.

00:14:42.260 --> 00:14:43.290
Okay!

00:14:43.290 --> 00:14:47.100
We'll take down Cosmos with our triplet combination.

00:14:47.100 --> 00:14:48.530
Just you three?

00:14:48.530 --> 00:14:50.800
Well, just leave it to us.

00:14:53.810 --> 00:14:55.940
Shimizu-san, it's terrible!

00:14:55.940 --> 00:14:56.670
What's wrong?

00:14:56.670 --> 00:14:58.880
Just get over here!

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:02.980
Eh? 11-4!?

00:15:02.980 --> 00:15:04.080
What's going on?

00:15:04.080 --> 00:15:09.150
I'm sorry. They got 8 goals on the Cosmos in an instant.

00:15:09.150 --> 00:15:13.890
So we switched with Girasol.

00:15:13.890 --> 00:15:19.630
And now Girasol scored 4 goals, but they scored 3 in return?

00:15:19.630 --> 00:15:22.730
Those triplets are amazing.

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:24.800
Frightening amazing.

00:15:28.040 --> 00:15:29.270
Focus! Focus!

00:15:47.030 --> 00:15:47.360
Nice!

00:15:47.360 --> 00:15:48.760
Yes!

00:15:48.760 --> 00:15:50.130
That's enough!

00:15:51.630 --> 00:15:55.430
You're really good! That last shot just now was amazing.

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:59.140
Misaki-san, we have a request.

00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:02.010
Please let us play Rosa.

00:16:02.010 --> 00:16:04.110
You will let us, right?

00:16:04.110 --> 00:16:07.450
Otherwise, there would be no point in us being here.

00:16:07.450 --> 00:16:09.610
What kind of training did you do?

00:16:09.610 --> 00:16:12.420
We saw the video of your friendly match in America.

00:16:12.420 --> 00:16:17.920
We learned from that match and played against a middle school team.

00:16:19.220 --> 00:16:20.790
We're serious.

00:16:20.790 --> 00:16:21.960
I know.

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:24.700
Cosmos and Girasol both lost by large margins.

00:16:24.700 --> 00:16:27.630
If this keeps up, New Tokyo FC's reputation will be in shambles.

00:16:27.630 --> 00:16:29.830
But we won't be holding back.

00:16:29.830 --> 00:16:32.500
Gather around, Rosa!

00:16:50.620 --> 00:16:51.390
Wow!

00:17:48.980 --> 00:17:50.950
I know your tricks now.

00:18:07.530 --> 00:18:09.700
Wow!

00:18:09.700 --> 00:18:13.570
Hey! Why are you standing there!? What happened to your voice!?

00:18:13.570 --> 00:18:15.270
Oh yeah!

00:18:18.610 --> 00:18:21.850
Don't mind! Don't mind! We're still okay!

00:18:21.850 --> 00:18:23.280
We'll get back those goals!

00:18:23.280 --> 00:18:24.550
Go!

00:18:24.550 --> 00:18:27.390
They're using the same strategy against us.

00:18:27.390 --> 00:18:30.820
Well, we were copying them in the first place.

00:18:30.820 --> 00:18:35.090
It'll be tough if you three don't change tactics.

00:18:35.090 --> 00:18:37.630
No, we'll score.

00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:40.030
We'll prove to them that we aren't just boys.

00:18:40.030 --> 00:18:40.770
Eh?

00:18:40.770 --> 00:18:44.170
Please forgive our selfishness, just this once.

00:18:44.170 --> 00:18:46.340
Ouzou-kun! Kota-kun!

00:18:48.470 --> 00:18:49.440
Huh!?

00:18:55.250 --> 00:18:59.150
Our formation will be all messed up, so please take care of the defense.

00:18:59.150 --> 00:19:00.590
Eh? Okay...

00:19:03.020 --> 00:19:04.260
What are you doing!?

00:19:17.300 --> 00:19:18.070
Go!

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:52.500
Yes! Goal!

00:19:54.110 --> 00:19:55.540
You did it!

00:19:55.540 --> 00:20:00.080
Yes, but let's hope the same trick works again.

00:20:22.230 --> 00:20:24.940
Okay! That ends the match!

00:20:31.610 --> 00:20:33.710
Looks like we lost.

00:20:33.710 --> 00:20:37.580
We won on aggregate, 13-12.

00:20:37.580 --> 00:20:40.720
But against Rosa, it was 8-1. A complete defeat.

00:20:40.720 --> 00:20:46.290
Nope. It's our loss for only scoring 8 points on you.

00:20:46.290 --> 00:20:48.890
We also got scored on.

00:20:48.890 --> 00:20:51.530
But we lost, either way.

00:20:51.530 --> 00:20:53.900
No, it's our loss.

00:20:53.900 --> 00:20:55.600
You guys are amazing.

00:20:55.600 --> 00:20:59.170
With a good coach, you can get even better.

00:20:59.170 --> 00:21:01.370
Then please be our coach.

00:21:01.970 --> 00:21:04.680
Kota-kun, don't ask for the impossible.

00:21:04.680 --> 00:21:05.210
Huh?

00:21:05.210 --> 00:21:08.650
Professional players can't coach amateur teams.

00:21:08.650 --> 00:21:09.880
Right, Misaki-san?

00:21:09.880 --> 00:21:13.350
That's right, sorry about that.

00:21:14.590 --> 00:21:16.590
You're Erika-chan, right?

00:21:16.590 --> 00:21:17.620
Yes!

00:21:17.620 --> 00:21:22.230
Does the Namba Dandelion 
clubhouse still have that poster up?

00:21:22.230 --> 00:21:23.560
Yes, yes.

00:21:23.560 --> 00:21:25.530
This?

00:21:25.530 --> 00:21:27.270
Did you bring that from Osaka?

00:21:27.270 --> 00:21:32.240
No, this is a copy. I copied that poster.

00:21:32.240 --> 00:21:36.370
Actually I wrote those sloppy words.

00:21:36.370 --> 00:21:40.440
Eh? You were part of the Namba Dandelions?

00:21:40.440 --> 00:21:42.610
I was one of the founding members.

00:21:42.610 --> 00:21:45.280
I wrote that I wanted to be on the top of the world,

00:21:45.280 --> 00:21:50.120
but lost my chance due to injuries.

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:53.790
Even if I want to, I don't have the time to coach you guys.

00:21:53.790 --> 00:21:55.930
Please understand.

00:22:00.600 --> 00:22:04.000
We just need three more people to form a real team!

00:22:04.000 --> 00:22:08.270
We just have to keep on practicing like this and we can win the big tournaments!

00:22:08.270 --> 00:22:12.610
We can even be the best team in the country!

00:22:12.610 --> 00:22:16.050
All right! Let's find three more players!

00:22:16.050 --> 00:22:18.720
Then we can start training for real!

00:22:18.720 --> 00:22:19.650
Shou-kun.

00:22:19.650 --> 00:22:20.250
Huh?

00:22:20.250 --> 00:22:23.720
We never said we were going to keep on playing.

00:22:23.720 --> 00:22:26.090
We have achieved our goal.

00:22:26.090 --> 00:22:28.690
That's the end of our soccer, for now.

00:22:28.690 --> 00:22:31.860
It was pretty fun. Later.

00:22:31.860 --> 00:22:33.100
Bye.

00:22:33.870 --> 00:22:36.570
We finally have our team!

00:22:36.570 --> 00:22:40.740
Shou-kun, we have to prepare for our middle school entrance exams.

00:22:40.740 --> 00:22:42.140
Sorry about that.

00:22:42.140 --> 00:22:43.770
Later!

00:22:46.010 --> 00:22:50.550
It's great that the Furuyas joined us,

00:22:50.550 --> 00:22:54.050
but we need a proper coach or else we won't go anywhere!

00:22:54.050 --> 00:22:56.420
That's that. Later.

00:22:58.960 --> 00:23:02.790
Am I all alone again!?

00:23:02.790 --> 00:23:06.960
No way!

00:24:35.690 --> 00:24:38.590
My team is gone again!

00:24:38.590 --> 00:24:41.630
We can't revive without a coach.

00:24:41.630 --> 00:24:45.330
A coach? Let's ask that drunk person over there!

00:24:45.330 --> 00:24:47.330
That's too reckless!

00:24:47.330 --> 00:24:50.800
But this guy is pretty amazing!

00:24:50.800 --> 00:24:54.770
Next episode of Ginga e Kickoff! Lightning Light.

00:24:51.670 --> 00:24:54.770
「Lightning Light」

00:24:51.670 --> 00:24:54.770
「Lightning Light」
